<% content_for :title, 'Edit Subsector' %>

<%= render 'help/page', title: 'Edit Subsector' do %>
  <div class='space-y-6'>
    <div>
      <dl class='space-y-5'>
        <div>
          <dt class='font-semibold text-fg-bright'>Name</dt>
          <dd class='mt-1 text-fg'>The subsector&rsquo;s designation. Use <i class="fa-regular fa-dice"></i> generate a random name. Use <i class="fa-solid fa-language"></i> to set the language used to generate the name.</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt class='font-semibold text-fg-bright'>Observations</dt>
          <dd class='mt-1 text-fg'>Free-text notes in CommonMark (Markdown) format. Displayed on the subsector survey record.</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt class='font-semibold text-fg-bright'>Build Plan</dt>
          <dd class='mt-1 text-fg'>
            YAML configuration that controls how this subsector is procedurally generated.
            See the <%= link_to 'build specification reference', help_page_path('subsector_build_specification'), class: 'no-underline hover:underline hover:underline-offset-2' %> for the full schema.
          </dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt class='font-semibold text-fg-bright'>Derive Build from Survey</dt>
          <dd class='mt-1 text-fg'>
            <div class='space-y-3'>
              <p>The <span class="font-semibold text-fg-bright">Derive Build from Survey</span> button creates a build configuration
                that matches the existing sector data. This is useful when you want to generate a new version
                of the subsector but ensure that the same hexes have star systems and rogue objects.
              </p>
              <p>The derived build configuration preserves the structural outline of the subsector. It keeps:</p>
              <ul class='list-disc list-inside space-y-1'>
                <li>which hexes contain star systems</li>
                <li>the star types and the types of stellar bodies orbiting the stars</li>
                <li>the UWP for terrestrial planets</li>
                <li>the UWP for planetoid belts</li>
                <li>the size of gas giants</li>
                <li>which hexes contain rogue objects</li>
                <li>the types of rogue objects</li>
                <li>the names of objects</li>
              </ul>
              <p>Data that may change when generating the subsector will be the specific details about
                objects. For example, the atmospheric composition may be different, the number of moons or
                planetoids may change.</p>
            </div>
          </dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt class='font-semibold text-fg-bright'>Update sore</dt>
          <dd class='mt-1 text-fg'>
            Save the changes and return to the subsector view.
          </dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
    </div>

    <div class='pt-2 text-right uppercase font-mono text-xs tracking-[0.22em] text-fg-muted'>
      REFERENCE 0619SE
    </div>
  </div>
<% end %>
